# TopUp Build Logic (MUST FOLLOW)

> Native Android only. Plugin prefix: `topup.*`. Composite build: `build-logic/`.
> This repo does **not** use Phera/KMP plugins or six environment build types.

## Build types

- `:app` uses stock AGP **`debug`** and **`release` only**.
- Do **not** add `dev` / `stg` / `prod`, product flavors, or `developmentDebug`-style types.
- Libraries (`core/*`, `feature/*`) stay single-variant; no environment flavors.

## Convention plugins only in modules

```kotlin
// ✅
plugins {
    alias(libs.plugins.topup.android.library.compose)
    alias(libs.plugins.topup.serialization)
    alias(libs.plugins.topup.koin)
}

// ❌ raw AGP/Kotlin/Compose plugins or duplicated baseline Compose deps
```

| Module kind | Plugins |
|-------------|---------|
| `:app` | `topup.android.application.compose` + stack as needed |
| Compose library | `topup.android.library.compose` (+ stack) |
| Non-Compose library | `topup.android.library` (+ stack) |

### Stack plugins (opt-in)

`serialization` · `navigation` · `firebase` · `room` · `sqlcipher` · `datastore` · `ktor` · `koin` · `supabase` · `coroutines`

- `topup.ktor` also applies Serialization.
- `topup.supabase` needs `topup.ktor` on the same module.
- `topup.room` applies KSP + Room; pair `topup.sqlcipher` when encrypting the DB.
- Apply Android library/application convention **before** stack plugins that need AGP (e.g. Room).

Baseline SDK/Java 18/Compose/test deps live in configurers — modules only add project + module-specific libs.

## Secrets & signing

- Release signing keys in root `local.properties` (never commit): `RELEASE_KEYSTORE`, `RELEASE_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD`, `RELEASE_KEY_ALIAS`, `RELEASE_KEY_PASSWORD`.
- Supabase client keys in root `local.properties` (never commit): `SUPABASE_URL`, `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` → `:app` `BuildConfig.SUPABASE_URL` / `BuildConfig.SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`.
- Fail-hard at configuration if missing/invalid — owned by `AndroidApplicationConfigurer`.

## Layout & ownership

```
build-logic/convention/src/main/kotlin/
├── common/          # DefaultBuildConfig, PluginIds, JavaTargets (no BuildEnvironment)
├── configuration/   # *Configurer (Android DSL + stack deps)
├── plugins/         # Thin Plugin wrappers
└── utils/           # Catalog / Android / local.properties helpers
```

| Change | Where |
|--------|--------|
| SDK / app id / version / signing keys | `DefaultBuildConfig.kt` |
| App / library Android DSL | `AndroidApplicationConfigurer` / `AndroidLibraryConfigurer` |
| New stack | `*Configurer` + plugin + `gradlePlugin {}` + `PluginIds` + `libs.versions.toml` |

Keep plugins thin: `pluginManager.apply(...)` then configurer. Sync `PluginIds` ↔ `gradlePlugin` ↔ catalog.

## Anti-patterns

- KMP / Compose Multiplatform / `buildSrc` / Groovy DSL
- Inline versions outside `libs.versions.toml`
- `afterEvaluate` for variant wiring; duplicating signing/minify outside app configurer
- Applying `com.android.application` to `core/*` or `feature/*`

## Verify

```bash
./gradlew :build-logic:convention:validatePlugins
./gradlew :app:assembleDebug :app:assembleRelease
```
